# Part I

---

# 1. Purpose

The Feature Engine is responsible for transforming validated market data into deterministic model inputs suitable for both research and production trading.

Its purpose is to ensure that every feature produced by the platform is:

* deterministic
* reproducible
* traceable
* version controlled
* mathematically defined
* free from future information leakage
* identical between research and live execution

The Feature Engine is the only authorized subsystem responsible for producing model-ready features.

No model may compute its own features independently.

This guarantees that research, backtesting, simulation, paper trading, and live trading consume identical feature definitions.

---

# 2. Scope

Version 1 supports only production features required by the single production trading model.

The scope includes:

* market-derived features
* derived statistical features
* rolling window calculations
* normalization
* feature validation
* feature metadata
* feature registry
* deterministic feature generation

The Feature Engine does **not** include:

* feature discovery algorithms
* automated feature generation
* online feature learning
* feature marketplaces
* distributed feature computation
* cross-strategy feature sharing
* reinforcement learning features

These capabilities remain outside Version 1.

---

# 3. Objectives

The Feature Engine shall satisfy the following objectives.

## 3.1 Determinism

Every feature generated from identical source data shall always produce identical values.

No randomness is permitted.

---

## 3.2 Reproducibility

Historical experiments shall recreate identical feature datasets regardless of execution date.

---

## 3.3 Consistency

Research and production shall consume the same feature implementation.

Duplicate implementations are prohibited.

---

## 3.4 Traceability

Every feature shall be attributable to:

* its mathematical definition
* implementation version
* source datasets
* configuration
* creation timestamp
* owner

---

## 3.5 Simplicity

Version 1 prioritizes a small set of well-understood production features instead of maximizing feature count.

Quality is preferred over quantity.

---

# 4. Engineering Philosophy

The Feature Engine follows six engineering principles.

## Principle 1 — Features Are Products

Features are treated as production assets rather than temporary research artifacts.

Every production feature has:

* documentation
* owner
* identifier
* validation
* lifecycle

---

## Principle 2 — Single Source of Truth

Every feature shall have exactly one implementation.

Alternative implementations are prohibited.

---

## Principle 3 — Mathematical Transparency

Every production feature shall possess a documented mathematical definition.

Researchers must understand exactly how a feature is calculated.

Black-box feature generation is prohibited.

---

## Principle 4 — Deterministic Computation

Feature computation shall depend only on:

* historical market data
* approved configuration
* deterministic mathematical operations

External runtime conditions shall never influence results.

---

## Principle 5 — Research Before Production

New features shall undergo research validation before entering production.

Production features are stable engineering artifacts rather than experimental ideas.

---

## Principle 6 — Minimal Complexity

Version 1 intentionally limits production features to approximately 10–15 carefully validated signals.

Adding additional features requires measurable evidence of improved production performance.

---

