Production feature behavior shall be governed through approved configuration rather than source code modifications.

Configuration may define:

* rolling window lengths
* thresholds
* normalization parameters
* operational limits

Configuration shall not redefine the mathematical meaning of a production feature.

Changing computational behavior requires a new feature version.

---

## Configuration Principles

Configuration shall be:

* deterministic
* version controlled
* immutable during execution
* reproducible

Runtime modification of production configuration is prohibited.

---

## REQ-FEAT-059

Feature configuration shall be version controlled.

---

## REQ-FEAT-060

Runtime modification of production feature configuration is prohibited.

