# 39. Failure Handling

Feature generation failures shall be treated as operational failures rather than recoverable computation events.

If a production feature cannot be generated correctly, downstream consumers shall not receive substituted values.

Failure handling shall prioritize correctness over availability.

Permitted responses include:

* fail the feature
* fail the feature batch
* suspend model inference
* generate operational alerts

Automatic approximation is prohibited.

---

## REQ-FEAT-061

Feature computation failures shall prevent publication to the Feature Store.

---

## REQ-FEAT-062

Production systems shall never substitute failed feature values automatically.

